-- coa1-part4-capacity.l4: Part 4 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), A company's capacity and related matters, ss 39 to 52
-- (lines 425-563 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively; every rule cites its provision with @ref and quotes the text
-- on `-- src:` lines (generated from the raw file by srcrefs.py quote). See the header of coa1-part2-formation.l4 for how to read
-- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING and for the two kinds of function ("requirement met" and "the duty arises").
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script;
-- it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- SEAMS. s 42(1) is computed here and read by ss 39 and 40 as a MAYBE BOOLEAN input named for it: JUST TRUE means "section 42 takes the
-- act out of section 39 (or 40)", JUST FALSE means "section 42 does not (the exception applies, or the section does not extend to the
-- company)", NOTHING means "section 42 says nothing (the company is not a charity)". s 252 (connected with a director) and s 1121 (in default)
-- are other parts' answers, taken as MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs. Every NOT is bracketed: `NOT a OR b` reads as `NOT (a OR b)` on the stable binary.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 4: A COMPANY'S CAPACITY AND RELATED MATTERS (lines 425-563)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 39: A company's capacity --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:427 | 39 A company's capacity
-- src:428 | (1) The validity of an act done by a company shall not be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity by reason of anything in the company's constitution.
-- src:429 | (2) This section has effect subject to section 42 (companies that are charities).
@ref s 39(1) A company's capacity: validity not called into question (src:427-429)
GIVEN `the ground is lack of capacity by reason of anything in the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under s 42(1) that section 39 does not apply to the act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) the validity of the act can be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity` MEANS
    IF NOT `the ground is lack of capacity by reason of anything in the company's constitution`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "the ground of lack of capacity by reason of anything in the company's constitution"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the answer under s 42(1) that section 39 does not apply to the act`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to section 42 (companies that are charities)" and section 42 takes the act out of section 39
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The validity of an act done by a company shall not be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity by reason of anything in the company's constitution"

-- ---- s 40: Power of directors to bind the company --------------------------------------------------------

-- src:432 | (2) For this purpose—
-- src:433 | (a) a person “deals with” a company if he is a party to any transaction or other act to which the company is a party,
@ref s 40(2) Power of directors to bind the company: "deals with" (src:432-433)
GIVEN `the person is a party to a transaction or other act to which the company is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2)(a) the person deals with the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party to a transaction or other act to which the company is a party`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person “deals with” a company if he is a party to any transaction or other act to which the company is a party" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))

-- src:434 | (b) a person dealing with a company—
-- src:435 | (i) is not bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors to bind the company or authorise others to do so,
@ref s 40(2) Power of directors to bind the company: a person dealing is not bound to enquire (src:434-435)
GIVEN `the person deals with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
