    IF `the person deals with the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person dealing with a company— (i) is not bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors to bind the company or authorise others to do so"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person dealing with a company"

-- src:436 | (ii) is presumed to have acted in good faith unless the contrary is proved, and
@ref s 40(2) Power of directors to bind the company: presumed good faith (src:436-436)
GIVEN `the person deals with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2)(b)(ii) the person dealing with the company is presumed to have acted in good faith` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person deals with the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person dealing with a company"
    ELSE IF `the contrary is proved`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is presumed to have acted in good faith unless the contrary is proved"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:437 | (iii) is not to be regarded as acting in bad faith by reason only of his knowing that an act is beyond the powers of the directors under the company's constitution.
@ref s 40(2) Power of directors to bind the company: knowledge that an act is beyond the directors' powers (src:437-437)
GIVEN `the person deals with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
