    IF `the person deals with the company` AND `the person knows that an act is beyond the powers of the directors under the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to be regarded as acting in bad faith by reason only of his knowing that an act is beyond the powers of the directors under the company's constitution"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative is for "a person dealing with a company" who knows "that an act is beyond the powers of the directors"

-- src:430 | 40 Power of directors to bind the company
