    IF NOT `the person deals with the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In favour of a person dealing with a company in good faith"
    ELSE IF `the contrary to good faith is proved`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In favour of a person dealing with a company in good faith"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the answer under s 42(1) that section 40 does not apply to the act`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to ... section 42 (companies that are charities)" and section 42 takes the act out of section 40
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

