-- src:450 | (2) Where—
-- src:451 | (a) a company enters into such a transaction, and
-- src:452 | (b) the parties to the transaction include—
-- src:453 | (i) a director of the company or of its holding company, or
-- src:454 | (ii) a person connected with any such director,
-- src:455 | the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company.
@ref s 41(2) Transactions involving directors or their associates: voidable at the instance of the company (src:450-455)
GIVEN `section 41 applies to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company enters into the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party to the transaction is a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 252 a party to the transaction is a person connected with such a director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`section 41 applies to the transaction` AND `the company enters into the transaction`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a company enters into such a transaction, and (b) ..., the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company" (the rule applies only where)
    ELSE IF `a party to the transaction is a director of the company or of its holding company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 252 a party to the transaction is a person connected with such a director`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— ... (b) the parties to the transaction include— (i) a director of the company or of its holding company, or (ii) a person connected with any such director, the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company" (the rule applies only where)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a person connected with a director" has the same meaning as in Part 10 (s 41(7)(b))

-- src:456 | (3) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party to the transaction as is mentioned in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (ii), and any director of the company who authorised the transaction, is liable—
-- src:457 | (a) to account to the company for any gain he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction, and
-- src:458 | (b) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction.
