    CONSIDER `the answer under s 41(3) that the person is liable`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `any gain the person has made directly or indirectly by the transaction, in pounds`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person other than a director of the company is not liable under subsection (3) if he shows that at the time the transaction was entered into he did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers" (s 41(5)): nil is what the person must pay
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the liability is stated for "any such party ... and any director of the company who authorised the transaction"

@ref s 41(3) Transactions involving directors or their associates: to indemnify against loss (src:458-458)
