    ELSE IF NOT `the company is a charity`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 39 and 40 ... do not apply to the acts of a company that is a charity", and the text is silent on a company that is not
         ELSE IF `the person does not know at the time the act is done that the company is a charity` OR (`the person gives full consideration in money or money's worth in relation to the act` AND `the person does not know that the act is beyond the powers of the directors`)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to the acts of a company that is a charity except in favour of a person who— (a) does not know at the time the act is done that the company is a charity, or (b) gives full consideration in money or money's worth ... and does not know ... (ii) that the act is beyond the powers of the directors"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:476 | (2) Where a company that is a charity purports to transfer or grant an interest in property, the fact that (as the case may be)—
-- src:477 | (a) the act was not permitted by the company's constitution, or
-- src:478 | (b) the directors in connection with the act exceeded any limitation on their powers under the company's constitution,
-- src:479 | does not affect the title of a person who subsequently acquires the property or any interest in it for full consideration without actual notice of any such circumstances affecting the validity of the company's act.
@ref s 42(2) Companies that are charities: title of a person who acquires property (src:476-479)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company purports to transfer or grant an interest in property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person subsequently acquires the property or an interest in it for full consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acquires it without actual notice of any circumstances affecting the validity of the company's act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not extend to Scotland"
    ELSE IF       `the company is a charity`
              AND `the company purports to transfer or grant an interest in property`
              AND `the person subsequently acquires the property or an interest in it for full consideration`
              AND `the person acquires it without actual notice of any circumstances affecting the validity of the company's act`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the title of a person who subsequently acquires the property or any interest in it for full consideration without actual notice of any such circumstances affecting the validity of the company's act"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names only a person who acquires "for full consideration without actual notice" from a charity company that purports to transfer or grant an interest

-- src:480 | (3) In any proceedings arising out of subsection (1) or (2) the burden of proving—
-- src:481 | (a) that a person knew that the company was a charity, or
-- src:482 | (b) that a person knew that an act was not permitted by the company's constitution or was beyond the powers of the directors,
-- src:483 | lies on the person asserting that fact.
@ref s 42(3) Companies that are charities: the burden of proof (src:480-483)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the fact is that a person knew that the company was a charity, or that a person knew that an act was not permitted by the company's constitution or was beyond the powers of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person asserting that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(3) the burden of proving the fact lies on the person` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not extend to Scotland"
    ELSE IF NOT `the fact is that a person knew that the company was a charity, or that a person knew that an act was not permitted by the company's constitution or was beyond the powers of the directors`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the burden is stated for the two facts in paragraphs (a) and (b)
         ELSE IF `the person is the person asserting that fact`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the burden of proving— (a) that a person knew that the company was a charity, or (b) that a person knew that an act was not permitted by the company's constitution or was beyond the powers of the directors, lies on the person asserting that fact"

-- src:484 | (4) In the case of a company that is a charity the affirmation of a transaction to which section 41 applies (transactions with directors or their associates) is ineffective without the prior written consent of—
-- src:485 | (a) in England and Wales, the Charity Commission;
-- src:486 | (b) in Northern Ireland, the Department for Social Development.
@ref s 42(4) Companies that are charities: affirmation of a transaction (src:484-486)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 41 applies to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prior written consent of the Charity Commission (England and Wales) or the Department for Social Development (Northern Ireland) has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not extend to Scotland"
    ELSE IF NOT (`the company is a charity` AND `section 41 applies to the transaction`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company that is a charity the affirmation of a transaction to which section 41 applies"
         ELSE IF `the prior written consent of the Charity Commission (England and Wales) or the Department for Social Development (Northern Ireland) has been given`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says the affirmation "is ineffective without" the consent and does not say that with it the affirmation is effective
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the affirmation of a transaction to which section 41 applies (transactions with directors or their associates) is ineffective without the prior written consent of— (a) in England and Wales, the Charity Commission; (b) in Northern Ireland, the Department for Social Development"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Formalities of doing business under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland (lines 488-526)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 43: Company contracts -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:489 | 43 Company contracts
-- src:490 | (1) Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a contract may be made—
-- src:491 | (a) by a company, by writing under its common seal, or
-- src:492 | (b) on behalf of a company, by a person acting under its authority, express or implied.
@ref s 43(1) Company contracts: how a contract may be made (src:489-492)
GIVEN `the contract is made under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is made by the company, by writing under its common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is made on behalf of the company, by a person acting under its authority, express or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(1) the contract may be made in that way` MEANS
    IF `the contract is made under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` AND (`the contract is made by the company, by writing under its common seal` OR `the contract is made on behalf of the company, by a person acting under its authority, express or implied`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a contract may be made— (a) by a company, by writing under its common seal, or (b) on behalf of a company, by a person acting under its authority, express or implied"

-- src:493 | (2) Any formalities required by law in the case of a contract made by an individual also apply, unless a contrary intention appears, to a contract made by or on behalf of a company.
@ref s 43(2) Company contracts: formalities required of an individual (src:493-493)
GIVEN `the contract is made by or on behalf of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law requires formalities in the case of a contract made by an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(2) the formalities required of an individual apply to the contract` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the contract is made by or on behalf of a company`) OR (NOT `the law requires formalities in the case of a contract made by an individual`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any formalities required by law in the case of a contract made by an individual also apply ... to a contract made by or on behalf of a company"
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a contrary intention appears"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 44: Execution of documents ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:494 | 44 Execution of documents
-- src:495 | (1) Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a document is executed by a company—
-- src:496 | (a) by the affixing of its common seal, or
-- src:497 | (b) by signature in accordance with the following provisions.
@ref s 44(1) Execution of documents: how a document is executed (src:494-497)
GIVEN `the document is executed under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's common seal is affixed to the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed in accordance with section 44(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(1) the document is executed by the company` MEANS
    IF `the document is executed under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` AND (`the company's common seal is affixed to the document` OR `the document is signed in accordance with section 44(2)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a document is executed by a company— (a) by the affixing of its common seal, or (b) by signature in accordance with the following provisions" (no "only")

-- src:498 | (2) A document is validly executed by a company if it is signed on behalf of the company—
-- src:499 | (a) by two authorised signatories, or
-- src:500 | (b) by a director of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature.
@ref s 44(2) Execution of documents: signature on behalf of the company (src:498-500)
GIVEN `the number of authorised signatories who sign the document on behalf of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `a director of the company signs the document on behalf of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(2) signature in that way validly executes the document for the company` MEANS
    IF `the number of authorised signatories who sign the document on behalf of the company` AT LEAST 2 OR `a director of the company signs the document on behalf of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document is validly executed by a company if it is signed on behalf of the company— (a) by two authorised signatories, or (b) by a director of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a); sealing is the other route, s 44(1)(a))

-- src:501 | (3) The following are “authorised signatories” for the purposes of subsection (2)—
-- src:502 | (a) every director of the company, and
-- src:503 | (b) in the case of a private company with a secretary or a public company, the secretary (or any joint secretary) of the company.
@ref s 44(3) Execution of documents: authorised signatories (src:501-503)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company with a secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the secretary or a joint secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(3) the person is an authorised signatory for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the person is the secretary or a joint secretary of the company` AND (`the company is a public company` OR `the company is a private company with a secretary`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following are “authorised signatories” for the purposes of subsection (2)— (a) every director of the company, and (b) ..." (no "only")

-- src:504 | (4) A document signed in accordance with subsection (2) and expressed, in whatever words, to be executed by the company has the same effect as if executed under the common seal of the company.
@ref s 44(4) Execution of documents: same effect as the common seal (src:504-504)
GIVEN `the document is signed in accordance with section 44(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is expressed, in whatever words, to be executed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(4) the document has the same effect as if executed under the common seal of the company` MEANS
    IF `the document is signed in accordance with section 44(2)` AND `the document is expressed, in whatever words, to be executed by the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document signed in accordance with subsection (2) and expressed, in whatever words, to be executed by the company has the same effect as if executed under the common seal of the company"

-- src:505 | (5) In favour of a purchaser a document is deemed to have been duly executed by a company if it purports to be signed in accordance with subsection (2).
-- src:506 | A “purchaser” means a purchaser in good faith for valuable consideration and includes a lessee, mortgagee or other person who for valuable consideration acquires an interest in property.
@ref s 44(5) Execution of documents: a purchaser (src:505-506)
GIVEN `the person is a purchaser in good faith for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a lessee, mortgagee or other person who for valuable consideration acquires an interest in property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(5) the person is a purchaser` MEANS
    IF `the person is a purchaser in good faith for valuable consideration` OR `the person is a lessee, mortgagee or other person who for valuable consideration acquires an interest in property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “purchaser” means a purchaser in good faith for valuable consideration and includes a lessee, mortgagee or other person who for valuable consideration acquires an interest in property"

@ref s 44(5) Execution of documents: deemed due execution in favour of a purchaser (src:505-505)
GIVEN `the person is a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document purports to be signed in accordance with section 44(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(5) the document is deemed to have been duly executed by the company in favour of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a purchaser` AND `the document purports to be signed in accordance with section 44(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In favour of a purchaser a document is deemed to have been duly executed by a company if it purports to be signed in accordance with subsection (2)"

-- src:507 | (6) Where a document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more than one company, it is not duly signed by that person for the purposes of this section unless he signs it separately in each capacity.
@ref s 44(6) Execution of documents: a person signing for more than one company (src:507-507)
GIVEN `the document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more than one company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person signs it separately in each capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(6) the document is duly signed by the person for the purposes of section 44` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more than one company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more than one company"
    ELSE IF `the person signs it separately in each capacity`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is not duly signed ... unless he signs it separately in each capacity": the text says what is not duly signed and not that the document is duly signed once the "unless" is met (fork F-unless)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not duly signed by that person for the purposes of this section unless he signs it separately in each capacity"

-- src:508 | (7) References in this section to a document being (or purporting to be) signed by a director or secretary are to be read, in a case where that office is held by a firm, as references to its being (or purporting to be) signed by an individual authorised by the firm to sign on its behalf.
@ref s 44(7) Execution of documents: an office held by a firm (src:508-508)
GIVEN `the office of director or secretary is held by a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed (or purports to be signed) by an individual authorised by the firm to sign on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(7) the document is read as signed by the director or secretary` MEANS
    IF `the office of director or secretary is held by a firm` AND `the document is signed (or purports to be signed) by an individual authorised by the firm to sign on its behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case where that office is held by a firm, as references to its being (or purporting to be) signed by an individual authorised by the firm to sign on its behalf"

-- src:509 | (8) This section applies to a document that is (or purports to be) executed by a company in the name of or on behalf of another person whether or not that person is also a company.
@ref s 44(8) Execution of documents: executed in the name of or on behalf of another person (src:509-509)
GIVEN `the document is (or purports to be) executed by a company in the name of or on behalf of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(8) this section applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is (or purports to be) executed by a company in the name of or on behalf of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether or not that other person is also a company
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a document that is (or purports to be) executed by a company in the name of or on behalf of another person"

-- ---- s 45: Common seal -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:518 | (6) This section does not form part of the law of Scotland.
@ref s 45(6) Common seal: not the law of Scotland (src:518-518)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(6) this section forms part of the law that applies to the company` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not form part of the law of Scotland" (read as a company registered in Scotland, fork F-s45)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names only the law of Scotland

-- src:510 | 45 Common seal
-- src:511 | (1) A company may have a common seal, but need not have one.
@ref s 45(1) Common seal: a company may have a common seal but need not (src:510-511)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(1) the company may have a common seal` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not form part of the law of Scotland" (s 45(6))
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 45(1) Common seal: a company need not have a common seal (src:511-511)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(1) the company need have a common seal` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not form part of the law of Scotland" (s 45(6))
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may have a common seal, but need not have one"

-- src:512 | (2) A company which has a common seal shall have its name engraved in legible characters on the seal.
@ref s 45(2) Common seal: the company's name engraved on the seal (src:512-512)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(2) the company must have its name engraved in legible characters on its common seal` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not form part of the law of Scotland" (s 45(6))
    ELSE IF `the company has a common seal`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company which has a common seal shall have its name engraved in legible characters on the seal" (the duty arises only for a company which has a common seal)

DECLARE `s 45(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 45(2) engrave the company's name in legible characters on the common seal`

@ref s 45(2) Common seal: the company's duty (src:512-512)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 45(2) action`
`s 45(2) the company's duty to engrave its name on its common seal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 45(2) the company must have its name engraved in legible characters on its common seal` place `the company has a common seal`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY Company
        MUST `s 45(2) engrave the company's name in legible characters on the common seal`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company has a common seal that does not have its name engraved in legible characters"
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- src:513 | (3) If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) an offence is committed by—
-- src:514 | (a) the company, and
-- src:515 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 45(3) Common seal: offence by the company (src:513-515)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's name is engraved in legible characters on the seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not form part of the law of Scotland" (s 45(6))
    ELSE IF `the company has a common seal` AND (NOT `the company's name is engraved in legible characters on the seal`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) an offence is committed by— (a) the company" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))

@ref s 45(3) Common seal: offence by an officer in default (src:513-515)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's name is engraved in legible characters on the seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not form part of the law of Scotland" (s 45(6))
    ELSE IF NOT (`the company has a common seal` AND (NOT `the company's name is engraved in legible characters on the seal`))
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is committed by "every officer of the company who is in default" and the text is silent on an officer who is not
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an officer is in default is s 1121's answer

-- src:516 | (4) An officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company, commits an offence if he uses, or authorises the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company on which its name is not engraved as required by subsection (2).
@ref s 45(4) Common seal: using a seal on which the name is not engraved (src:516-516)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the person is an officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses, or authorises the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's name is not engraved on the seal as required by subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF place EQUALS `Scotland`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not form part of the law of Scotland" (s 45(6))
    ELSE IF `the person is an officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company` AND `the person uses, or authorises the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company` AND `the company's name is not engraved on the seal as required by subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company, commits an offence if he uses, or authorises the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company on which its name is not engraved as required by subsection (2)" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 45(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 45(4) an officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company`

DECLARE `s 45(4) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 45(4) use, or authorise the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company on which its name is not engraved`

@ref s 45(4) Common seal: the prohibition (src:516-516)
`s 45(4) the prohibition` MEANS
    PARTY `s 45(4) an officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company`
    SHANT `s 45(4) use, or authorise the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company on which its name is not engraved`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 45(4) an officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company` BECAUSE "the person used, or authorised the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company on which its name is not engraved"

-- src:517 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 45(5) Common seal: the penalty (src:517-517)
`s 45(5) the penalty` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 45(5) Common seal: the most the person can be fined (src:517-517)
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45(5) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` MEANS
    `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

-- ---- s 46: Execution of deeds ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:519 | 46 Execution of deeds
-- src:520 | (1) A document is validly executed by a company as a deed for the purposes of section 1(2)(b) of the Law of Property (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1989 (c. 34) and for the purposes of the law of Northern Ireland if, and only if—
-- src:521 | (a) it is duly executed by the company, and
-- src:522 | (b) it is delivered as a deed.
@ref s 46(1) Execution of deeds: validly executed as a deed (src:519-522)
GIVEN `the document is duly executed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is delivered as a deed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(1) the document is validly executed by the company as a deed` MEANS
    IF `the document is duly executed by the company` AND `the document is delivered as a deed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document is validly executed by a company as a deed ... if, and only if— (a) it is duly executed by the company, and (b) it is delivered as a deed"

-- src:523 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) a document is presumed to be delivered upon its being executed, unless a contrary intention is proved.
@ref s 46(2) Execution of deeds: presumed delivery (src:523-523)
GIVEN `the document has been executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(2) the document is presumed to be delivered` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document has been executed`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a document is presumed to be delivered upon its being executed" ("upon" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention is proved`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a contrary intention is proved"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 47: Execution of deeds or other documents by attorney ---------------------------------------------

-- src:524 | 47 Execution of deeds or other documents by attorney
-- src:525 | (1) Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a company may, by instrument executed as a deed, empower a person, either generally or in respect of specified matters, as its attorney to execute deeds or other documents on its behalf.
@ref s 47(1) Execution by attorney: empowering an attorney (src:524-525)
GIVEN `the company empowers the person as its attorney under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the empowerment is by instrument executed as a deed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(1) the company may empower the person as its attorney to execute deeds or other documents on its behalf` MEANS
    IF `the company empowers the person as its attorney under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` AND `the empowerment is by instrument executed as a deed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a company may, by instrument executed as a deed, empower a person, either generally or in respect of specified matters, as its attorney"

-- src:526 | (2) A deed or other document so executed, whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere, has effect as if executed by the company.
@ref s 47(2) Execution by attorney: effect of a deed or other document so executed (src:526-526)
GIVEN `the deed or other document is executed by a person empowered under section 47(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(2) the deed or other document has effect as if executed by the company` MEANS
    IF `the deed or other document is executed by a person empowered under section 47(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A deed or other document so executed, whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere, has effect as if executed by the company"

-- ---- s 48: Execution of documents by companies (Scotland) ------------------------------------------------
-- s 48(1) ("The following provisions form part of the law of Scotland only") is an extent provision: inert under reason 2.

-- src:528 | 48 Execution of documents by companies
-- src:529 | (1) The following provisions form part of the law of Scotland only.
-- src:530 | (2) Notwithstanding the provisions of any enactment, a company need not have a company seal.
@ref s 48(2) Execution of documents by companies (Scotland): no company seal needed (src:528-530)
GIVEN `the law of Scotland applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2) the company need have a company seal` MEANS
    IF `the law of Scotland applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notwithstanding the provisions of any enactment, a company need not have a company seal"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following provisions form part of the law of Scotland only"

-- src:531 | (3) For the purposes of any enactment—
-- src:532 | (a) providing for a document to be executed by a company by affixing its common seal, or
-- src:533 | (b) referring (in whatever terms) to a document so executed,
-- src:534 | a document signed or subscribed(or, in the case of an electronic document, authenticated) by or on behalf of the company in accordance with the provisions of the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995 (c. 7) has effect as if so executed.
@ref s 48(3) Execution of documents by companies (Scotland): signed or subscribed (src:531-534)
GIVEN `the law of Scotland applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment provides for a document to be executed by a company by affixing its common seal, or refers to a document so executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed or subscribed (or, if electronic, authenticated) by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed, subscribed or authenticated in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(3) the document has effect as if executed by the affixing of the common seal` MEANS
    IF       `the law of Scotland applies`
         AND `the enactment provides for a document to be executed by a company by affixing its common seal, or refers to a document so executed`
         AND `the document is signed or subscribed (or, if electronic, authenticated) by or on behalf of the company`
         AND `the document is signed, subscribed or authenticated in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a document signed or subscribed (or, in the case of an electronic document, authenticated) by or on behalf of the company in accordance with the provisions of the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995 has effect as if so executed" (the Act of 1995 is outside the sources: its answer is an input)

-- ---- s 49: Official seal for use abroad ------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:536 | 49 Official seal for use abroad
-- src:537 | (1) A company that has a common seal may have an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom.
@ref s 49(1) Official seal for use abroad: a company may have one (src:536-537)
GIVEN `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(1) the company may have an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom` MEANS
    IF `the company has a common seal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): fork F43, a grant limited to "A company that has a common seal" by a relative clause, a scope limit with no "only" (the other reading is JUST FALSE): "A company that has a common seal may have an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom"

-- src:538 | (2) The official seal must be a facsimile of the company's common seal, with the addition on its face of the place or places where it is to be used.
@ref s 49(2) Official seal for use abroad: what it must be (src:538-538)
GIVEN `the official seal is a facsimile of the company's common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official seal has on its face the place or places where it is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(2) the official seal meets the requirements` MEANS
    IF `the official seal is a facsimile of the company's common seal` AND `the official seal has on its face the place or places where it is to be used`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The official seal must be a facsimile of the company's common seal, with the addition on its face of the place or places where it is to be used" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:539 | (3) The official seal when duly affixed to a document has the same effect as the company's common seal.
-- src:540 | This subsection does not extend to Scotland.
@ref s 49(3) Official seal for use abroad: same effect as the common seal (src:539-540)
GIVEN `the law of Scotland applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official seal is duly affixed to a document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(3) the official seal has the same effect as the company's common seal` MEANS
    IF `the law of Scotland applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection does not extend to Scotland"
    ELSE IF `the official seal is duly affixed to a document`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The official seal when duly affixed to a document has the same effect as the company's common seal" ("when" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- src:541 | (4) A company having an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom may—
-- src:542 | (a) by writing under its common seal, or
-- src:543 | (b) as respects Scotland, by writing subscribedor authenticated in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995,
-- src:544 | authorise any person appointed for the purpose to affix the official seal to any deed or other document to which the company is party.
@ref s 49(4) Official seal for use abroad: authorising a person to affix it (src:541-544)
GIVEN `the company has an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is given by writing under the company's common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as respects Scotland, the authority is given by writing subscribed or authenticated in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed for the purpose of affixing the official seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(4) the company may authorise the person to affix the official seal` MEANS
    IF `the company has an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom` AND `the person is appointed for the purpose of affixing the official seal` AND (`the authority is given by writing under the company's common seal` OR `as respects Scotland, the authority is given by writing subscribed or authenticated in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company having an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom may— (a) by writing under its common seal, or (b) as respects Scotland, by writing subscribed or authenticated ..., authorise any person appointed for the purpose to affix the official seal"

-- src:545 | (5) As between the company and a person dealing with such an agent, the agent's authority continues—
-- src:546 | (a) during the period mentioned in the instrument conferring the authority, or
-- src:547 | (b) if no period is mentioned, until notice of the revocation or termination of the agent's authority has been given to the person dealing with him.
@ref s 49(5) Official seal for use abroad: how long the agent's authority continues (src:545-547)
GIVEN `the question is as between the company and a person dealing with the agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the period mentioned in the instrument conferring the authority (if a period is mentioned)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which notice of the revocation or termination of the agent's authority was given to the person dealing with the agent (if it has been)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` MEANS
    IF NOT `the question is as between the company and a person dealing with the agent`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As between the company and a person dealing with such an agent"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the end of the period mentioned in the instrument conferring the authority (if a period is mentioned)`
         WHEN JUST periodEnd THEN
             IF `the date in question` AT MOST periodEnd
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the agent's authority continues— (a) during the period mentioned in the instrument conferring the authority" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `the date on which notice of the revocation or termination of the agent's authority was given to the person dealing with the agent (if it has been)`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST noticeDate THEN
                 IF `the date in question` LESS THAN noticeDate
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no period is mentioned, until notice of the revocation or termination of the agent's authority has been given to the person dealing with him" ("until": the bar ends on the day the notice is given, fork F-s49)

DECLARE `s 49(6) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal`

DECLARE `s 49(6) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 49(6) certify in writing on the deed or other document the date on which, and place at which, the official seal is affixed`

-- src:548 | (6) The person affixing the official seal must certify in writing on the deed or other document to which the seal is affixed the date on which, and place at which, it is affixed.
@ref s 49(6) Official seal for use abroad: certifying the date and place (src:548-548)
GIVEN `the person certifies in writing on the deed or other document the date on which the official seal is affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person certifies in writing on the deed or other document the place at which the official seal is affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and place` MEANS
    IF `the person certifies in writing on the deed or other document the date on which the official seal is affixed` AND `the person certifies in writing on the deed or other document the place at which the official seal is affixed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person affixing the official seal must certify in writing on the deed or other document to which the seal is affixed the date on which, and place at which, it is affixed" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

@ref s 49(6) Official seal for use abroad: the duty (src:548-548)
`s 49(6) the duty of the person affixing the official seal` MEANS
    PARTY `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal`
    MUST `s 49(6) certify in writing on the deed or other document the date on which, and place at which, the official seal is affixed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal` BECAUSE "the person affixing the official seal did not certify in writing the date on which, and place at which, it was affixed"

-- ---- s 50: Official seal for share certificates etc ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:549 | 50 Official seal for share certificates etc
-- src:550 | (1) A company that has a common seal may have an official seal for use—
-- src:551 | (a) for sealing securities issued by the company, or
-- src:552 | (b) for sealing documents creating or evidencing securities so issued.
@ref s 50(1) Official seal for share certificates: a company may have one (src:549-552)
GIVEN `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official seal is for sealing securities issued by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official seal is for sealing documents creating or evidencing securities so issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1) the company may have an official seal for the use` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has a common seal`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): fork F44, a grant limited to "A company that has a common seal" by a relative clause, a scope limit with no "only" (the other reading is JUST FALSE): "A company that has a common seal may have an official seal for use— (a) for sealing securities issued by the company, or (b) for sealing documents creating or evidencing securities so issued"
    ELSE IF `the official seal is for sealing securities issued by the company` OR `the official seal is for sealing documents creating or evidencing securities so issued`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "for use— (a) for sealing securities issued by the company, or (b) for sealing documents creating or evidencing securities so issued"

-- src:553 | (2) The official seal—
-- src:554 | (a) must be a facsimile of the company's common seal, with the addition on its face of the word “Securities”, and
-- src:555 | (b) when duly affixed to the document has the same effect as the company's common seal.
@ref s 50(2) Official seal for share certificates: what it must be and its effect (src:553-555)
GIVEN `the official seal is a facsimile of the common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official seal has on its face the word "Securities"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2)(a) the official seal meets the requirements` MEANS
    IF `the official seal is a facsimile of the common seal` AND `the official seal has on its face the word "Securities"`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The official seal— (a) must be a facsimile of the common seal, with the addition on its face of the word “Securities”" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

@ref s 50(2) Official seal for share certificates: effect when duly affixed (src:555-555)
GIVEN `the official seal is duly affixed to the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2)(b) the official seal has the same effect as the company's common seal` MEANS
    IF `the official seal is duly affixed to the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The official seal— ... (b) when duly affixed to the document has the same effect as the company's common seal" ("when" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- ---- s 51: Pre-incorporation contracts, deeds and obligations --------------------------------------------

-- src:556 | 51 Pre-incorporation contracts, deeds and obligations
-- src:557 | (1) A contract that purports to be made by or on behalf of a company at a time when the company has not been formed has effect, subject to any agreement to the contrary, as one made with the person purporting to act for the company or as agent for it, and he is personally liable on the contract accordingly.
@ref s 51(1) Pre-incorporation contracts: the person acting is personally liable (src:556-557)
GIVEN `the contract purports to be made by or on behalf of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the company has not been formed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an agreement to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(1) the person purporting to act for the company is personally liable on the contract` MEANS
    IF NOT `the contract purports to be made by or on behalf of a company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A contract that purports to be made by or on behalf of a company"
    ELSE IF NOT `at the time the company has not been formed`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A contract that purports to be made by or on behalf of a company at a time when the company has not been formed" ("when" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
         ELSE IF `there is an agreement to the contrary`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "has effect, subject to any agreement to the contrary, as one made with the person purporting to act for the company or as agent for it, and he is personally liable on the contract accordingly"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:558 | (2) Subsection (1) applies—
-- src:559 | (a) to the making of a deed under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland, and
-- src:560 | (b) to the undertaking of an obligation under the law of Scotland,
-- src:561 | as it applies to the making of a contract.
@ref s 51(2) Pre-incorporation contracts: deeds and obligations (src:558-561)
GIVEN `the act is the making of a deed under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the undertaking of an obligation under the law of Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the making of a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(2) subsection (1) applies to the act` MEANS
    IF `the act is the making of a deed under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` OR `the act is the undertaking of an obligation under the law of Scotland` OR `the act is the making of a contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) applies— (a) to the making of a deed ..., and (b) to the undertaking of an obligation ..., as it applies to the making of a contract"

-- ---- s 52: Bills of exchange and promissory notes --------------------------------------------------------

-- src:562 | 52 Bills of exchange and promissory notes
-- src:563 | A bill of exchange or promissory note is deemed to have been made, accepted or endorsed on behalf of a company if made, accepted or endorsed in the name of, or by or on behalf or on account of, the company by a person acting under its authority.
@ref s 52 Bills of exchange and promissory notes (src:562-563)
GIVEN `the instrument is a bill of exchange or promissory note` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is made, accepted or endorsed in the name of, or by or on behalf or on account of, the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is so made, accepted or endorsed by a person acting under the company's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52 the bill or note is deemed to have been made, accepted or endorsed on behalf of the company` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is a bill of exchange or promissory note` AND `the instrument is made, accepted or endorsed in the name of, or by or on behalf or on account of, the company` AND `the instrument is so made, accepted or endorsed by a person acting under the company's authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A bill of exchange or promissory note is deemed to have been made, accepted or endorsed on behalf of a company if made, accepted or endorsed in the name of, or by or on behalf or on account of, the company by a person acting under its authority" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))
